    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe old membership *tier* was a derived read-only property (`GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) computed from the owner's own fields and surfaced on the response via the generated `OwnerDto`. I replaced it with a numeric `membershipLevel`, keeping each piece of logic in the class that already owns it:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced `getMembershipTier()` (String) with `getMembershipLevel()` (Integer): starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. The cap leaves level 4 free for the reserved tenure case. This is the single home for the derivation, so the mapper and audit both read from it rather than duplicating the rule.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` string-enum schema for a `membershipLevel` integer (1\u20133, read-only). Since `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec and MapStruct maps by name, the response now carries `membershipLevel` and the old field is gone from the contract.\n\n3. **`service/OwnerAuditor.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=\u2026` (reading `owner.getMembershipLevel()`) in place of the tier, so the audit trail reflects the new value.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (asserting `$.membershipLevel == 3` for an owner with an email and no namesakes) passes, and no `membershipTier` references remain anywhere in the sources or generated code.\n\nA note on one judgment call: the spec said \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead.\" The existing create audit line did **not** actually record the tier \u2014 it logged id/customerCode/registrationDate only. I added `membershipLevel` to it to satisfy the spec's explicit intent that creation-time auditing capture the level; no test pins the exact audit format, so this is safe. Let me know if you'd prefer the audit line left untouched.",
